<title>UK: Smithkline, LG Chemical sign deal.</title>
<headline>Smithkline, LG Chemical sign deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>British drug group Smithkline Beecham said on Monday it had signed an agreement with Korea's LG Chemical to develop a novel broad spectrum antibiotic.  </p>
<p>The company said the drug, which has completed its early stage trials in Europe, had the potential &quot;to become the once-daily drug of choice for treatment of respiratory infections&quot;.</p>
<p>It said it believed the compound, codenamed LB20304a,  could build on the success of its best selling antibiotic 'Aaugmentin'.</p>
